## What was approved

Repointing the project board and switcher from `MergedProject` onto `ProjectWithStats`, including
deletion of three frontend files:
- `frontend/src/hooks/useMergedProjects.ts`
- `frontend/src/components/projects/LocationBadges.tsx`
- `frontend/src/components/projects/ProjectTypeFilter.tsx`

plus the rewrite of ~23 references to the dropped fields `has_local`, `local_project_id`, `nodes`
across `ProjectList.tsx`, `UnifiedProjectCard.tsx`, and `ProjectSwitcher.tsx`.

## Facts surfaced at the gate before approval

- All three dropped fields have been CONSTANTS since node-foundations (`merged.rs` hardcodes
  `has_local: true`, `local_project_id: Some(project.id)`, `nodes: Vec::new()`), so:
  - `LocationBadges` renders `project.nodes` — it has been rendering nothing.
  - `ProjectTypeFilter`'s "swarm" tab has always matched zero projects.
  - The `!has_local` branches are dead code.
- Blast radius verified: `has_local` appears in exactly the four files in `files:`; `MergedProject`
  has exactly six consumers, all in `files:`.
- All STOP triggers verified clear before dispatch (F2/F4).
- `/api/merged-projects` and `MergedProject` SURVIVE this task (deleted by 303), so the old path
  remains available if the new board misbehaves.
- Task 301's endpoint was proven by five hollow-test experiments plus a runtime probe showing both
  endpoints returning identical shared fields.

Decision: **approve — run 302**, pause again before 303.
